# IMPERIA COLD WAR — SSR concept English narrative revision.
"""Authored country-facing prose, kept separate from mechanical review records."""

COMMON={
'secretariat':"Our republic stands between the ambitions of its people and the demands of a continental Union. The republican administration must turn ministries, local councils and industrial managers into a government capable of securing investment and delivering what it promises.",
'moscow_cadres':"Officials with experience in the Union ministries know where allocations are decided and which signatures open doors. Bringing them into our administration will strengthen those connections, although republican priorities may receive less generous consideration when the centre issues its instructions.",
'local_cadres':"Administrators who know our towns, farms and factories can see difficulties that disappear in distant reports. Promoting them will give republican institutions deeper roots, while obliging us to accommodate influential local networks and their expectations.",
'appointment_school':"An expanding administration cannot depend indefinitely on personal recommendations and hurried appointments. Schools for public officials will teach accounting, industrial management and the practical work of government, creating a professional service beneath the political leadership.",
'audit_staff':"A fulfilled target on paper is of little use when machinery stands idle and the promised deliveries never arrive. Independent teams of accountants and engineers will examine enterprise books and public appointments, challenging the protections that have sheltered poor management.",
'discipline_campaign':"Warnings and quiet transfers have allowed too many officials to mistake their positions for private property. A concentrated disciplinary campaign will replace compromised administrators and reassert central authority, even if the upheaval briefly unsettles factories and local institutions.",
'complaints_office':"Workers and residents often know about shortages long before a ministry acknowledges them. A republican petitions office will bring those complaints into the administration and make local officials answer for abuses that have been dismissed as unavoidable difficulties.",
'plan_bargain':"Every investment programme begins with a contest over scarce machinery, building materials and skilled labour. Our delegation will present a coherent republican case to the Union ministries, replacing scattered requests with priorities that the centre can recognise and fund.",
'priority_orders':"The Union's strategic programmes offer large and dependable orders to enterprises willing to meet demanding specifications. Giving those contracts priority will strengthen military production, while leaving fewer resources for the goods and services consumed by our own households.",
'local_retention':"A republic cannot prosper solely by supplying distant customers while its own infrastructure and consumer industries wait. A larger share of investment will be directed towards republican needs, accepting a smaller role in the most prestigious military contracts.",
'successor_training':"Public administration should survive the retirement of any one official. Experienced department heads will train younger administrators and share responsibility for major projects, giving the republic a second rank capable of maintaining policy through a change of leadership.",
'controlled_debate':"Scientists, writers and experienced managers have arguments that deserve a hearing before they become grievances. A carefully widened public debate will bring fresh expertise into republican policy, at the price of a less obedient political atmosphere.",
'unified_line':"Conflicting instructions waste time and encourage officials to evade responsibility. A clear common line will bind the administration to a single programme, although experts who question its assumptions may find fewer opportunities to influence decisions.",
'republican_statute':"The responsibilities of ministries, local councils and republican departments have accumulated through custom as much as law. A revised administrative statute will clarify their powers and settle disputes before another development programme is delayed by competing claims.",
'union_delegate':"The republic needs a delegation that can defend its interests through more than occasional appeals to personal contacts. A permanent staff will follow Union deliberations, negotiate administrative disputes and keep republican priorities before the central institutions.",
'economic_accounts':"Reports assembled to satisfy production targets do not always reveal the condition of an economy. A republican survey of deliveries, employment and enterprise accounts will expose the shortages hidden behind impressive totals and give future investment a firmer basis.",
'combine_priority':"A modern industrial combine can gather workshops, skilled labour and technical services around a single productive centre. Concentrated investment promises a stronger manufacturing base, but its appetite for power, transport and imported machinery will be substantial.",
'consumer_priority':"Households judge economic progress by the goods they can obtain rather than the tonnage reported by heavy industry. Expanding consumer supply and distribution will answer those expectations, drawing investment away from military production and larger industrial monuments.",
'enterprise_accounts':"Enterprises need to know what their inputs cost and whether their customers can use the goods they deliver. Revised accounting will reward usable production and expose chronic losses, while retaining the wider economic obligations of the republican plan.",
'output_incentives':"Managers respond to the standards by which their factories are judged. Production incentives will reward technically demanding deliveries and sustained use of machinery, strengthening output while increasing the pressure on fuel, materials and maintenance services.",
'quality_contracts':"A component that fails inspection can delay production far beyond the factory that made it. Contracts based on reliability and quality will encourage better tools and supervision, even where meeting those standards slows the rush to fulfil a numerical target.",
'rail_depots':"Factories cannot operate on promises when freight waits in crowded depots. Better loading facilities and a stronger republican transport corridor will move machinery, fuel and agricultural goods with fewer interruptions, tying local production more securely to its customers.",
'rural_processing':"Too much of the value of a harvest is lost between the farm and the market. Storage, processing and reliable maintenance services will turn agricultural production into food and industrial inputs that can be delivered throughout the year.",
'machine_tools':"The quality of a workshop depends on the machinery with which its workers must contend. A programme of machine-tool renewal will give our engineers the means to improve precision and introduce more demanding production methods.",
'service_networks':"A productive enterprise still needs depots, wholesalers and dependable records of what has been ordered. Strengthening the distribution network will reduce the losses between producer and customer and bring more of the republic's economic activity into reliable accounts.",
'new_power':"Industrial expansion has outgrown generating capacity in too many places. Investment in conventional power will support new workshops and more dependable public services, binding the republic to a larger fuel supply and a continuing maintenance commitment.",
'energy_savings':"The cheapest additional power is often the power that need no longer be wasted. Metering, insulation and industrial energy audits will restrain demand, although enterprises must accept the cost and inconvenience of changing familiar production routines.",
'maintenance_stocks':"A missing bearing or damaged transformer can stop machinery worth far more than the spare part itself. Protected maintenance stocks and scheduled repairs will make industrial investment more dependable without another race to announce new construction.",
'diversify_orders':"Reliance on a narrow set of Union customers leaves the republic exposed whenever priorities change. Developing alternative suppliers and a broader civilian order book will sacrifice some immediate military output in exchange for a more resilient economy.",
'deepen_specialisation':"Concentrating on the products our Union customers need most can bring large orders and access to specialised machinery. That efficiency comes with dependence: a change in procurement or the breakdown of common supply arrangements would leave a difficult industrial inheritance.",
'plan_settlement':"An investment cycle is complete only when its enterprises can work reliably after the construction brigades have departed. Permanent production standards and stronger commercial accounts will turn the plan's accumulated improvements into an enduring republican asset.",
'social_accounts':"Schools, clinics and housing offices form the daily face of government. A review of their staffing, expenditure and reach will show where republican promises can be sustained and where an overstretched service is merely concealing its failures.",
'technical_institutes':"Modern production requires engineers able to understand complex machinery and improve it. Strengthening the technical institutes will give the republic greater scientific capacity, while committing public funds to institutions whose benefits take years to mature.",
'vocational_schools':"A skilled mechanic can keep an entire workshop in production. Vocational schools will concentrate on maintenance, machine operation and practical technical instruction, supplying the workers and specialists needed by an expanding industrial economy.",
'housing_repairs':"Leaking roofs, overcrowded apartments and unreliable heating undermine confidence in even the most ambitious development plan. Repairing existing housing will bring visible improvements to daily life, with costs that cannot be hidden behind the announcement of a new estate.",
'republican_culture':"Language, literature and local institutions give the republic a public life of its own. Supporting them will deepen attachment to republican government, while requiring accommodation between communities whose expectations of cultural policy do not always coincide.",
'union_curriculum':"Common technical standards make it easier for graduates to study, work and serve throughout the Union. A more uniform curriculum will strengthen those connections, leaving less room for the educational priorities defended by local cultural institutions.",
'public_health':"Preventive medicine and accessible clinics can answer needs that prestigious hospitals alone cannot meet. A stronger local health service will improve confidence in republican institutions, provided the budget can sustain its staff, supplies and facilities.",
'collective_farms':"Agriculture cannot meet rising demand with worn machinery and unreliable repairs. Modern equipment and permanent service workshops will raise the capacity of the collective sector, at the cost of additional energy use and a larger investment commitment.",
'household_plots':"Small plots and local markets already supply goods that the larger agricultural system struggles to deliver. Giving them a wider place in food provision will improve supply, while making production and revenue more difficult for the state to supervise.",
'water_accounts':"Irrigation, factories and growing towns all draw upon the same rivers and land. A republican account of water use and soil damage will reveal costs that individual enterprises have been able to pass on to their neighbours.",
'environmental_controls':"An enterprise's success should not be measured by the pollution it can leave for another district to endure. Enforceable limits on industrial waste and water use will protect agriculture and settlements, even when established producers demand exemptions.",
'remediation_fund':"Closing every polluting enterprise would leave the republic with another economic crisis. A dedicated remediation fund will repair damaged facilities and finance cleaner processes while keeping viable plants in operation.",
'service_settlement':"Public guarantees will endure only if their administration becomes more efficient. A lasting settlement will preserve essential services while reducing avoidable expenditure, replacing emergency appeals and competing departmental promises with a credible republican commitment.",
'civil_registers':"Reliable civil records make public administration possible beyond the offices of a handful of experienced officials. Modern registers and trained local staff will strengthen services, revenue collection and the authority of republican institutions.",
'defence_commission':"The republic supplies personnel, workshops and transport to a much larger military system. A defence commission will coordinate that contribution with civilian development, ensuring that Union requirements do not arrive as contradictory demands upon local institutions.",
'military_components':"Defence orders reward factories that can maintain exacting standards over long production runs. Dedicated component workshops will give the republic a stronger place in military procurement and a correspondingly larger demand for power and specialised inputs.",
'dual_use_industry':"Civilian engineering and military supply share many tools and skills. Workshops able to serve both markets will broaden the republic's industrial base, accepting less concentration on dedicated arms production in return for greater flexibility.",
'technical_reserves':"Military equipment depends on mechanics, radio operators and technical specialists as much as frontline units. Reserve training will prepare those skills within the republican population and strengthen the personnel base available to the Union commands.",
'specialist_training':"Longer technical instruction can produce personnel capable of handling more complex equipment and responsibilities. The republic will favour competence over rapid throughput, accepting a slower training cycle in return for greater professional cohesion.",
'mass_training':"A broad reserve requires a training system that can reach beyond a small professional core. Shorter, standardised courses will prepare more personnel quickly, while leaving advanced instruction to later service and specialised schools.",
'military_repairs':"Different repair practices and incomplete technical records turn minor faults into lengthy absences from service. Common maintenance standards will give workshops a dependable supply of documentation and make scarce spare parts go further.",
'civil_shelters':"Modern war would reach far beyond the barracks. Shelters, warning systems and emergency exercises will prepare the civilian administration for disruption and give the public greater confidence in the republic's ability to protect daily life.",
'strategic_transport':"The same bridges and freight connections serve industrial production and military mobilisation. Improving a strategic transport corridor will strengthen both, provided civilian traffic is not left waiting whenever defence requirements receive priority.",
'officer_education':"Technical warfare demands officers able to understand logistics, communications and the equipment under their command. Better access to military education will prepare republican personnel for responsibilities that cannot be mastered through routine service alone.",
'fuel_discipline':"Fuel disappears quickly through poor maintenance, careless handling and unnecessary movement. A stricter service regime will reduce those losses, though units must devote more time to inspections and technical instruction.",
'ready_stocks':"Units recover more quickly when spare parts, instructors and maintenance personnel are available before an exercise begins. Financing that readiness will strengthen sustained training while increasing the cost of the military establishment.",
'defence_records':"Personnel lists and maintenance obligations should survive a transfer of command. Complete defence records will protect the republic from competing claims and preserve the technical knowledge upon which any future military administration must depend.",
'combined_exercises':"Combined exercises test whether transport, technical services and trained personnel can work together under Union command. The lessons will be carried home by officers and specialists whose experience matters long after the last vehicle returns to its depot.",
'public_authority':"Independence has placed the responsibilities of a state in republican hands. Ministries must answer to a national government, local authorities need a clear chain of responsibility, and citizens must see more than a new emblem above familiar offices.",
'citizenship_civic':"The republic is home to people whose languages and memories cross its new frontiers. Equal citizenship will bind those communities to a common state, demanding an administration prepared to serve them without making ancestry the test of belonging.",
'citizenship_restoration':"Independence has revived claims that Soviet law had buried beneath the authority of the Union. A restoration settlement will give the state a firmer historical foundation, while raising difficult questions for residents whose lives were built under the previous order.",
'rights_commission':"A new constitution will mean little if ordinary citizens cannot challenge an official's decision. A national rights commission will hear grievances and establish procedures capable of surviving the political passions of the independence movement.",
'unitary_services':"The new state cannot afford a separate bargain with every provincial administration. A unified public service will concentrate resources and authority, accepting the resentment of local institutions that have grown accustomed to defending their own prerogatives.",
'local_guarantees':"A durable republic must leave room for its regions and communities to recognise themselves within national institutions. Negotiated local guarantees will broaden consent, at the cost of a more demanding and politically divided administration.",
'revenue_service':"Old payments to Union institutions have ended before a reliable national tax service has taken their place. Trained inspectors, clear accounts and enforceable collection procedures will give the treasury the means to support an independent government.",
'court_review':"The officials of a sovereign republic must be subject to its law. Independent courts will review public appointments and administrative decisions, breaking inherited protections while limiting the executive's freedom to settle disputes by decree.",
'executive_service':"A fractured administration needs an executive capable of issuing instructions that will actually be carried out. Concentrating responsibility will bring greater discipline to public affairs, while narrowing the avenues through which independent institutions can challenge the cabinet.",
'registered_accounts':"The treasury needs a national account of what public institutions owe and what they are entitled to collect. Settling those obligations will replace uncertain claims with a fiscal system upon which ministries, enterprises and local authorities can plan.",
'social_compact':"Workers and pensioners should not be asked to accept independence as a promise that their livelihoods will be considered later. A national social compact will protect basic commitments while requiring the treasury and major employers to confront their true cost.",
'payment_register':"The disappearance of common payment arrangements has left enterprises holding invoices that their former customers cannot settle. A national register of commercial arrears will separate recoverable claims from debts that are keeping the whole economy in suspense.",
'gradual_conversion':"Viable enterprises can fail when a temporary shortage of working capital becomes a chain of missed payments. Bridge credit will preserve essential production while new contracts are negotiated, leaving the treasury to distinguish rescue from another indefinite subsidy.",
'rapid_conversion':"Arrears cannot serve indefinitely as a substitute for payment. A firm settlement of unpaid contracts will release resources for viable businesses, although creditors, workers and entire industrial towns may bear the losses when old promises are written off.",
'supplier_contracts':"The old plan allocated components without asking each enterprise to negotiate a foreign contract. New commercial agreements must establish prices, payment and dependable delivery, rebuilding the practical connections on which production still relies.",
'worker_ownership':"Workers know which parts of their enterprises can be saved and which managers have been hiding failure. Giving them a voice in reconstruction will protect practical knowledge and social confidence, while making rapid changes of ownership or production more difficult.",
'open_tenders':"Public contracts and industrial restructuring should attract more than the same circle of well-connected managers. Open tenders will bring new capital and commercial standards, with little comfort for enterprises that can no longer win orders through political access.",
'industrial_conversion':"The republic has inherited factories built for customers and suppliers now beyond its borders. Retooling, new standards and better commercial accounts will turn that industrial inheritance towards orders that can sustain production in an independent economy.",
'budget_protection':"Public services carry the expectations of a population already facing economic upheaval. Protecting them will preserve confidence and household security, but the government must raise dependable revenue and postpone investments it can no longer finance at once.",
'budget_consolidation':"A sovereign treasury cannot meet every obligation inherited from the Union system. A concentrated fiscal adjustment will reduce administrative commitments and rebuild revenue, accepting the immediate political cost of withdrawing promises the state cannot sustain.",
'commercial_standards':"Markets need records, enforceable contracts and banks that can distinguish a viable enterprise from a politically protected debtor. Common commercial standards will make transactions more dependable and bring economic activity back within the reach of public institutions.",
'export_conversion':"Factories accustomed to a guaranteed order book must learn to satisfy customers who can buy elsewhere. Export conversion will finance new standards and product lines, opening markets while exposing established enterprises to a harsher commercial test.",
'domestic_chains':"Local suppliers can keep a factory working when foreign payments and deliveries fail. Rebuilding those connections will make the economy more resilient, although smaller production runs and duplicated facilities demand additional capital and energy.",
'transition_settlement':"Reconstruction must leave behind institutions capable of preventing another cycle of arrears and emergency subsidies. A lasting economic settlement will bring public accounts, commercial law and industrial policy into a coherent national framework.",
'defence_authority':"The defence of the republic now rests with its own government. A national ministry must establish civilian responsibility, settle personnel obligations and turn inherited military offices into an administration that can support a sovereign chain of command.",
'professional_force':"A smaller professional establishment can concentrate instructors, technical specialists and reliable equipment where they are most useful. Its cohesion will come at a substantial personnel cost and a slower path towards a larger army.",
'territorial_force':"Territorial service ties defence to communities throughout the republic. A broad reserve will prepare local protection and mobilisation, while accepting less uniform instruction and weaker cohesion than a concentrated professional force.",
'maintenance_command':"A new flag does not provide spare parts, trained mechanics or a dependable pay system. A national maintenance command will bring those responsibilities together and give the armed forces a practical foundation beneath their formal independence.",
'local_officers':"The republic needs officers whose careers and professional loyalties are rooted in its own institutions. A national officer school will train a new generation in command, technical service and the demands of maintaining a force the country can afford.",
'reserve_records':"Reservists cannot be mobilised effectively from incomplete lists and outdated addresses. A national reserve service will establish dependable records and training schedules, with a continuing burden on personnel and local administration.",
'defence_settlement':"Competing claims over command, maintenance and recruitment have left too much uncertainty in military affairs. A final administrative settlement will make responsibilities clear and allow defence planning to proceed beyond the immediate disputes of separation.",
'mobile_defence':"A mobile force can concentrate against threats before they become a fixed front. Training for manoeuvre will improve operational cohesion, while demanding more fuel, technical instruction and maintenance from a still limited defence budget.",
'prepared_defence':"Prepared positions and deliberate territorial planning can make a smaller force difficult to dislodge. The army will favour sustained defence over rapid movement, accepting the logistical burden of maintaining a wider defensive system.",
'foreign_service':"For decades, foreign affairs were conducted through the Union's embassies and central ministries. Our republic must now speak with its own voice. A professional diplomatic service will defend our interests abroad, negotiate access to markets and establish the relationships on which lasting independence depends.",
'old_market_offer':"The frontiers have changed, but our factories still depend on familiar customers and suppliers. A clearing convention with the former Union centre could preserve essential deliveries and settle commercial accounts, placing economic continuity above the resentments of separation.",
'new_market_offer':"New markets demand machinery, standards and commercial knowledge that our enterprises cannot acquire overnight. A technical partnership will invite outside expertise into reconstruction, exchanging part of our economic freedom for faster access to the means of modern production.",
'border_offer':"A frontier must become more than a line defended by suspicious officials. A joint border commission can regulate crossings, customs and practical disputes, preserving ordinary trade without allowing unresolved questions to poison every relationship with our neighbour.",
'training_offer':"Our armed forces need instructors and experience suited to their new responsibilities. A training convention with a capable partner will open military schools and technical cooperation, bringing outside influence into institutions whose independence remains politically sensitive.",
'civil_neutrality':"The republic can defend its independence without placing its security in the hands of another patron. A policy of armed neutrality will favour territorial readiness and civilian diplomacy, accepting the limits of a defence establishment built largely from domestic resources.",
'energy_offer':"Power stations, pipelines and factories were built for an interconnected economy. An energy and transit convention can keep those connections operating across new frontiers, giving both governments a practical interest in reliable deliveries and predictable charges.",
'river_offer':"Rivers do not end at the republic's frontier. Irrigation, reservoirs and industrial water supplies bind neighbouring states to one another. A shared commission will negotiate releases and conservation before seasonal shortages become a permanent source of political confrontation.",
'regional_service':"Neighbouring governments will judge the republic by its ability to honour practical agreements. Experienced diplomatic and technical staff will turn negotiations on trade, water and transport into relationships that can survive a disagreement between political leaders.",
}

def apply_common(c,profile):
    for n in c.NODES:
        if n['key'] in COMMON:n['description']=COMMON[n['key']]
    context=profile['context'].lower()
    regional={
      'regional_review':f"The economy of {profile['name']} has grown around {context}. The next investment programme must decide whether to strengthen that established role or build a broader base beneath the republic's future prosperity.",
      'regional_orders':f"{profile['regional_choices'][0]} draws on facilities and skills already woven into the Union economy. Modernisation can increase their value to major customers, while leaving the republic more exposed to the supply arrangements and procurement priorities that sustain them.",
      'regional_diversify':f"{profile['regional_choices'][1]} will give the republic a wider range of producers and customers. The immediate return may be less impressive than another expansion of its established specialisation, but local livelihoods will depend on fewer decisions taken elsewhere.",
      'regional_standards':"Inherited industrial and agricultural problems cannot be erased by announcing another investment plan. Technical supervision, maintenance and honest public accounts will reduce their cost and leave the republic better prepared to manage the consequences of its own development.",
    }
    for n in c.NODES:
        if n['group']=='regional':n['description']=regional[n['key']]
    for s in c.STARTING:
        s.pop('resolution',None)
    c.TRANSITION[2]['description']="Personnel, maintenance services and command offices were organised around the Union armed forces. Sovereignty has left the republic to settle those responsibilities while building institutions able to sustain a national defence establishment."
